#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:2
msgid "Data Spillage Handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/entry-adv.rst:7
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Entry and Enterprise Advanced "
"<https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__ plans"
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:6
msgid "plans-img-yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:7
msgid ""
"Data Spillage Handling helps prevent accidental data spillage and helps "
"system administrators respond quickly to potential leaks without "
"disrupting collaboration. Enabling this feature empowers Mattermost users"
" to report messages that may contain sensitive, regulated, or "
"inappropriate information, and enables designated content reviewers to "
"assess and take appropriate action by removing or dismissing quarantined "
"messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:9
msgid ""
"By making every team member a first line of defense against sensitive-"
"data exposure, Data Spillage Handling strengthens mission-critical, "
"secure deployments and supports compliance with organizational and "
"regulatory data-handling standards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:12
msgid "Before you begin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:14
msgid ""
"You must be a System Admin in Mattermost. You need to identify who will "
"be content reviewers for quarantined messages, and you need to decide "
"whether quarantined messages should be hidden from users in Mattermost "
"while under review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:17
msgid "Enable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:19
msgid ""
"Data Spillage Handling isn't enabled by default. To enable Data Spillage "
"Handling:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:21
msgid "Go to **System Console > Site Configuration > Data Spillage Handling**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:22
msgid "Set **Enable Data Spillage Handling** to **True**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:24
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can configure Data Spillage Handling via the "
":ref:`config.json file or through environment variables <administration-"
"guide/configure/site-configuration-settings:content flagging>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:27
msgid "Configure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:29
msgid "Under **Content Reviewers**, define who should review quarantined content:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:31
msgid ""
"**Same reviewers for all teams**: Set to **True** to apply one global "
"reviewer list across all teams, or **False** to configure reviewers per "
"team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:32
msgid ""
"**Reviewers**: Start typing to search for users to assign as content "
"reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:36
msgid ""
"Choose reviewers carefully. Assigning reviewer roles grants access to "
"potentially sensitive information and may expose data from private "
"channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:38
msgid ""
"A global reviewer can view quarantined messages from all teams and "
"channels, including private channels they’re not a member of."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:39
msgid ""
"Team-specific reviewers can view quarantined messages from their assigned"
" teams, including private channels within those teams they’re not members"
" of."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:41
msgid "**Additional reviewers**: Optionally include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:43
msgid ""
"**System Administrators**: System admins receive quarantined messages for"
" all teams they are part of."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:44
msgid ""
"**Team Administrators**: Team admins receive quarantined messages for "
"their respective teams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:46
msgid ""
"Under **Notification Settings**, specify who receives updates at each "
"stage of the quarantine workflow when content is quarantined or reviewed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:48
msgid "**Notify when content is quarantined**: Reviewer(s), Author."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:49
msgid "**Notify when a reviewer is assigned**: Reviewer(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:50
msgid "**Notify when content is removed**: Reviewer(s), Author, Reporter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:51
msgid "**Notify on dismissal**: Reviewer(s), Author, Reporter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:53
msgid ""
"All notifications are sent via the **Data Spillage Bot** as direct "
"messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:55
msgid ""
"Under **Additional Settings**, configure how the quarantine workflow "
"behaves:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:57
msgid ""
"**Reasons for quarantine**: Define the preset categories that appear in "
"the quarantine dialog for users (for example: **Classification "
"mismatch**, **Need-to-know violation**, **Personally identifiable "
"information (PII) exposure**, **Operational security (OPSEC) concern**, "
"**Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI) violation**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:58
msgid ""
"**Require reporters to add comment**: Set to **True** to require users to"
" add a short explanation when quarantining a message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:59
msgid ""
"**Require reviewers to add comment**: Set to **True** to require "
"reviewers to add a comment when resolving a quarantine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:60
msgid ""
"**Hide message from channel while it is being reviewed**: Set to **True**"
" to automatically hide quarantined messages from the channel until "
"reviews are complete. If a root post is quarantined, the entire thread is"
" hidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:63
msgid ""
"We recommend enabling **Hide message from channel while it is being "
"reviewed** and require comments from both reporters and reviewers to "
"maintain transparency, accountability, and an auditable record of "
"actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:66
msgid "Monitor quarantined messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:68
msgid ""
"When :doc:`a user quarantines a message </end-user-guide/collaborate"
"/flag-messages>`, the **Data Spillage Bot** sends a direct message to all"
" content reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:70
msgid ""
"Direct messages from the **Data Spillage Bot** is a centralized "
"moderation queue, where reviewers can view, assign, and act on "
"quarantined messages without leaving Mattermost. Reviewers can use it to "
"monitor potential data spills, coordinate response, and maintain an "
"auditable record of review activity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:72
msgid ""
"Each quarantined message appears as a card-formatted message that "
"includes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:74
msgid "**Quarantined by**: The user who reported the message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:75
msgid ""
"**Status**: The current state of the review. All quarantined content "
"starts in **Pending** status."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:76
msgid ""
"**Reason**: The reason selected by the reporter (for example, "
"**Classification mismatch**, **Need-to-know violation**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:77
msgid ""
"**Message preview**: A snippet of the quarantined message, including the "
"author, timestamp, and original channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:78
msgid ""
"**Reviewer**: The user currently assigned to review the message "
"(initially **Unassigned**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:79
msgid ""
"**Channel**: The name of the channel where the message was originally "
"posted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:80
msgid "**Team**: The team context for the quarantined message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:81
msgid "**Comment**: Any reporter-provided context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:82
msgid ""
"**Post ID**: The system identifier for the original message for auditing "
"purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:84
msgid "Reviewers can select **View details** to take action as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:86
msgid "Assign a **Reviewer** responsible for reviewing the quarantined message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:87
msgid ""
"**Remove message**: Permanently delete the quarantined message from its "
"original channel for all users. The status of the quarantined message "
"changes to **Removed**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:88
msgid ""
"**Keep message**: Dismiss the quarantine and restore the message if it "
"was hidden. The status of the quarantined message changes to "
"**Retained**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:89
msgid "**Add a comment**: Record the reason for the decision when required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:91
msgid ""
"Once an action is taken, the **Status** field updates automatically. The "
"**Data Spillage Bot** sends follow-up notifications to the reporter, "
"author, and other reviewers based on how Data Spillage Handling is "
"configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:94
msgid "Deleted messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:96
msgid ""
"When a reviewer permanently removes a quarantined message, the message "
"and all associated data are deleted from the database and can't be "
"recovered, including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:98
msgid ""
"Message content and properties: The text of the message and any "
"associated post properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:99
msgid ""
"File metadata: Information about files attached to the message (e.g., "
"file names, IDs, and links to storage)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:100
msgid ""
"File metadata from edit history: Information about files attached to "
"earlier versions of the message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:101
msgid "Edit history: All previous versions of the message and their timestamps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:102
msgid ""
"Uploaded files: The actual files stored in Mattermost’s file storage "
"(local, S3, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:103
msgid "Priority data: Any message priority or importance settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:104
msgid "Acknowledgements: Records of users who acknowledged the message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:105
msgid "Reminders: Any reminders created for the message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:108
msgid "Best practice recommendations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/content-flagging.rst:110
msgid ""
"Before rolling out Data Spillage Handling organization-wide, we recommend"
" communicating that the feature protects both users and the organization "
"from accidental data spillage. Start with a pilot team to validate "
"reviewer notifications and workflows, integrate the process with existing"
" data-handling or incident-response playbooks, and require reporter and "
"reviewer comments to ensure every decision is transparent and auditable."
msgstr ""

